 ## File layout
 
+By default, memory is scoped automatically to the current Git repository:
+
 ```
 ~/.pi/agent/memory/
-  MEMORY.md              # Curated long-term memory
-  SCRATCHPAD.md           # Checklist of things to fix/remember
-  daily/
-    2026-02-15.md         # Daily append-only log
-    2026-02-14.md
-    ...
-  recovery/
-    <recovery-id>.json    # Complete payload and restore state for a memory_forget deletion
-```
+  MEMORY.md              # Global memory used outside Git repositories
+  projects/
+    <project-key>/       # One isolated memory tree per repository
+      MEMORY.md
+      SCRATCHPAD.md
+      daily/
+      recovery/
+```
+
+Each project gets a separate qmd collection, so search cannot return memories
+from another repository. Git worktrees share the main repository's project key.
+Existing global files are not copied automatically; set `PI_MEMORY_PROJECT_SCOPE=0`
+or `PI_MEMORY_DIR` to keep using the legacy tree while migrating them.
 
