 ## Changelog
 
 See [CHANGELOG.md](./CHANGELOG.md).
+
+## Stable project identity (explicit, opt-in)
+
+The optional `~/.pi/agent/memory/project-identities.json` registry maps checkout
+roots to a shared project ID, independent of path or Git remote:
+
+```json
+{"version":1,"checkouts":{"/home/alice/project":"example-project","/Users/alice/project":"example-project"}}
+```
+
+Mapped checkouts use `projects/example-project/` and the qmd collection
+`pi-memory-example-project`. Worktrees use their main checkout's root. IDs must
+start with a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, digits and
+hyphens (at most 64 characters). Paths must be normalized and absolute.
+Missing registry/unmapped checkouts keep the existing path-derived scope;
+malformed registries fail closed. Explicit `PI_MEMORY_DIR` and
+`PI_MEMORY_PROJECT_SCOPE=0` retain their existing override semantics.
+
+This resolver does not migrate, merge or delete memory. Before enabling a map,
+review the checkout identities and copy/merge their histories into the chosen
+canonical scope with a separately verified migration. Changing a Git remote
+never changes the explicit identity. Do not infer identities from repo names
+or remote URLs: forks may intentionally have separate memory.
